	)
	(text_box "~{CM5_PWR_BTN} input:\n\nRasPi CM5: Pull low to force power off or power on from previous software powered off state. Internally pulled up to +5V via 10kΩ\n\nSTM32H7 CM5: Reset input, internally pulled up to +3V3 via 10kΩ\n\n\nCM5_BOOT input:\n\nRasPi CM5: A low on this pin forces booting from an RPI server (e.g. PC or a Raspberry Pi), if not used leave floating. Internally pulled up via 10kΩ to CM5_3.3V\n\nSTM32H7 CM5: BOOT0 input, internally pulled down to GND via 10kΩ"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 22.86 162.56 0)
		(size 50.8 25.4)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -0.0001)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.889 0.889)
				(color 132 0 132 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a2281254-5739-4f4f-b658-f374f8a751ae")
	)
	(text_box "Since ID_SD and ID_SC pins are used as GPIO pins, then to prevent the firmware from checking to see if there is a HAT EEPROM available, add force_eeprom_read=0 and disable_poe_fan=1 to the config.txt file."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 45.72 13.97 0)
		(size 43.815 6.985)
